From 92f2355eaa7a821334c8b304c9ec70afb4e6e061 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:51:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/57] hw/i2c, hw/sensor: AVR8X TWI host; ADXL345 and the
 Accel Click

- avr8x-twi: TWI host mode (DS40002324): bus state (IDLE forced by
  software), START/repeated START from MADDR, send/receive, ACKACT,
  MCMD REPSTART/RECVTRANS/STOP, smart mode, W1C flags, RIF/WIF host
  interrupt on the instance's second vector (TWIM), an I2C bus
  "twi0.i2c". Regenerated AVR64EA48 TWI tables (overlay
  twi_i2c_8bit_avr_v3.yaml: hooks on MCTRLA/B, MSTATUS, MADDR, MDATA).
- avr64ea48-cnano: the Nano Base's mikroBUS I2C on TWI0, so I2C Clicks
  (thermo8, accel) plug in there too.
- adxl345: ADXL345 data sheet Rev. G: register map and resets, I2C
  auto-increment, sampling at the BW_RATE rate on the virtual clock,
  full-resolution/10-bit/justified/clipped data with OFSx, DATA_READY,
  OVERRUN, WATERMARK (bypass), INT1/INT2 by INT_MAP and INT_INVERT; tap,
  activity, free fall, FIFO modes logged as not modelled. "x", "y", "z"
  in mg.
- mikrobus: "accel" (schematic v101): 0x53 (ADDR SEL on 0), INT1 on INT,
  CS R6 100k and RST R8 10k pull-ups.
- qtests: Accel on EXT1 (identity, standby, scaling, offsets, clipping,
  overrun, INT polarity and mapping); TWI host with the Accel and the
  Thermo 8 on the Nano Base.

Not checked against a physical Accel Click.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
